    {
      "id": "cy-LzpI",
      "step": 0,
      "order": 3,
      "family": "language",
      "title": "Language: Cyprus uses the Greek and English languages",
      "text": [
        "Cyprus uses the Greek and English languages. Greek has a unique alphabet not used in any other language. It shares similarities with both the Latin and [Cyrillic](https://www.plonkit.net/images/greece/greece_cyrillic.png) alphabets, however the lower case letters generally have softer shapes than the Cyrillic letters.",
        "NOTE: It goes without saying, but Greece also uses the Greek alphabet."
      ],
